hieve the desired visual offset. I\'m focusing on the top-right and bottom-left droplets. The top-right droplet\'s `-right` and `-top` values are being adjusted with more extreme values for larger screens. I\'m using `-right-4 sm:-right-8 md:-right-10 lg:-right-12 xl:-right-14` and `-top-5 sm:-top-8 md:-top-10 lg:-top-10`. The same logic is applied to the bottom-left droplet, with appropriate left and bottom adjustments. I\'m also ensuring the section padding and overflow are configured correctly.\n\n\n**Validating Droplet Visuals**\n\nI\'m verifying that the droplets do not cause horizontal scrolling on smaller devices. I\'ve adjusted the positioning, specifically `-right-3 sm:-right-6 md:-right-10 lg:-right-12` for the top-right and analogous values for the bottom-left droplet. I\'m also confirming the sizes of the droplets, with sizes from `32px` to `64px` and `46px` to `78px` respectively, work well on a tablet-sized screen.\n\n\n"
