    thinking: "**Analyzing User Iteration**\n\nI\'ve been examining the user\'s iterative process, specifically focusing on the positioning of the bottom-left droplet on `md`. The Git log reveals a pattern of testing and refinement. After multiple attempts with variations such as `-left-9`, `-left-14`, and `-left-2`, the user ultimately settled on `md:-left-8` for the final position.\n\n\n**Adjusting Screen Widths**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the requested width adjustments for the newsletter card container. The current mobile width is `max-w-[270px]`. I\'m considering smaller values, such as `max-w-[245px]` or `max-w-[250px]`, alongside `sm:max-w-[520px]`. For the tablet view, I\'m reducing `md:max-w-[820px]` to options like `md:max-w-[620px]` or `md:max-w-[640px]`, keeping in mind how that translates to desktop with options like `lg:max-w-[820px]` or `lg:max-w-[880px]`.\n\n\n**Refining Mobile & Tablet Widths**\n\nI\'ve been evaluating a `max-w-[245px]` container, considering padding and text size at each breakpoint. On tab screens, I find `md:text-3xl` proportionate in a `620px` card. Email form widths are also being adjusted; the `max-w-[220px]` works well on mobile. Lastly, I\'m checking droplet offsets in the new contexts, preserving the adjusted bottom-left position.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_162982"
